   "html": "<p>The DCF values Hershey at 218.59 dollars a share with a growth-in-perpetuity terminal value.</p>\n<p>It is the top of our DCF range and 36.5 percent above the 160.19 dollar share price. The Valuation section's sliders must reproduce it at the workbook's inputs.</p>\n<p>Check: Filed from the Milestone 4 DCF Valuation Memo. Not yet checked against the source; check it there, then set status to confirmed. Formula: (49,037.0 - 3,755.1) / 207.2 = 45,281.9 / 207.2 = 218.59. It is cell C77 (and M7) on the DCF 1-Pager tab.</p>\n<h3>Related</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/Terminal%20value%20by%20growth%20in%20perpetuity%2052,410.9%20million%20dollars\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/Terminal value by growth in perpetuity 52,410.9 million dollars\">Terminal value by growth in perpetuity 52,410.9 million dollars</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/Net%20debt%203,755.1%20million%20dollars\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/Net debt 3,755.1 million dollars\">Net debt 3,755.1 million dollars</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/Diluted%20shares%20207.2%20million\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/Diluted shares 207.2 million\">Diluted shares 207.2 million</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/DCF%20values%2036.5%20and%2020.5%20percent%20above%20share%20price\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/DCF values 36.5 and 20.5 percent above share price\">DCF values 36.5 and 20.5 percent above share price</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/Perpetuity%20and%20exit%20multiple%20values%20differ%20by%2025.57%20dollars%20a%20share\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/Perpetuity and exit multiple values differ by 25.57 dollars a share\">Perpetuity and exit multiple values differ by 25.57 dollars a share</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=01%20Sources/S9%20Team%20Q&amp;amp;D%20workbook%20for%20Hershey\" data-note=\"01 Sources/S9 Team Q&amp;amp;D workbook for Hershey\">S9 Team Q&amp;D workbook for Hershey</a></li>\n</ul>",
