   "html": "<p>The forecast years' unlevered free cash flows are worth 3,792.3 million dollars on October 5, 2026: 372.5 for the FY2026 stub, 1,759.1 for FY2027, and 1,660.7 for FY2028.</p>\n<p>It is the first stage of the DCF and only 7.7 percent of enterprise value by growth in perpetuity and 8.7 percent by exit multiple, so the forecast years matter less than the terminal value.</p>\n<p>Check: Filed from the Milestone 4 DCF Valuation Memo. Not yet checked against the source; check it there, then set status to confirmed. Formula: each year's free cash flow / (1 + 6.78%) ^ (days from the valuation date to its fiscal year end / 365), summed. It is cell C50 (and I50) on the DCF 1-Pager tab.</p>\n<h3>Related</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/Valuation%20date%205%20October%202026%20with%2023.9%20percent%20stub\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/Valuation date 5 October 2026 with 23.9 percent stub\">Valuation date 5 October 2026 with 23.9 percent stub</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/WACC%206.78%20percent\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/WACC 6.78 percent\">WACC 6.78 percent</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=02%20Atomic%20Notes/Terminal%20value%2092.3%20and%2091.3%20percent%20of%20enterprise%20value\" data-note=\"02 Atomic Notes/Terminal value 92.3 and 91.3 percent of enterprise value\">Terminal value 92.3 and 91.3 percent of enterprise value</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"wl\" href=\"#note=01%20Sources/S9%20Team%20Q&amp;amp;D%20workbook%20for%20Hershey\" data-note=\"01 Sources/S9 Team Q&amp;amp;D workbook for Hershey\">S9 Team Q&amp;D workbook for Hershey</a></li>\n</ul>",
